('473afe8a-ae2f-4372-9963-3808fd9a5b32', 131, 'Appointed for Lasting Fruit', 3, 'You did not choose me, but I chose you and appointed you so that you might go and bear fruit—fruit that will last.', 'John 15:16', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of divine purpose & calling, the truth of John 15:16 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "You did not choose me, but I chose you and appointed you so that you might go and bear fruit—fruit that will last." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on John 15:16, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in John 15:16. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that you did not choose me, but i chose you and appointed you so that you might go and bear fruit—fruit that will last. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
