('2daf793d-b5e0-4da8-bc0b-52bf6cb91327', 133, 'Finishing the Course with Joy', 3, 'However, I consider my life worth nothing to me; my only aim is to finish the race and complete the task the Lord Jesus has given me.', 'Acts 20:24', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of divine purpose & calling, the truth of Acts 20:24 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "However, I consider my life worth nothing to me; my only aim is to finish the race and complete the task the Lord Jesus has given me." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Acts 20:24, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Acts 20:24. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that however, i consider my life worth nothing to me; my only aim is to finish the race and complete the task the lord jesus has given me. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the 