('97e8cbc0-5c77-4a26-acd7-d96d1c20f4e2', 334, 'The Unmistakable Mark of Discipleship', 3, 'A new command I give you: Love one another. As I have loved you, so you must love one another. By this everyone will know that you are my disciples, if you love one another.', 'John 13:34-35', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of family, grace & covenant love, the truth of John 13:34-35 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "A new command I give you: Love one another. As I have loved you, so you must love one another. By this everyone will know that you are my disciples, if you love one another." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on John 13:34-35, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in John 13:34-35. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that a new command i give you: love one another. as i have loved you, so you must love one another. by this everyone will know that you are my disciples, if you love one another. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, 