('e40b95fe-bd22-4fa3-881e-50b175b32130', 339, 'The Joyful Shout of Belonging', 3, 'Shout for joy to the Lord, all the earth. Worship the Lord with gladness; come before him with joyful songs. Know that the Lord is God. It is he who made us, and we are his.', 'Psalm 100:1-3', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Psalm 100:1-3 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "Shout for joy to the Lord, all the earth. Worship the Lord with gladness; come before him with joyful songs. Know that the Lord is God. It is he who made us, and we are his." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Psalm 100:1-3, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Psalm 100:1-3. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that shout for joy to the lord, all the earth. worship the lord with gladness; come before him with joyful songs. know that the lord is god. it is he who made us, and we are his. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('649039b1-1a59-463b-9487-d04e5814afd9', 340, 'Rooted and Overflowing with Gratitude', 3, 'So then, just as you received Christ Jesus as Lord, continue to live your lives in him, rooted and built up in him, strengthened in the faith as you were taught, and overflowing with thankfulness.', 'Colossians 2:6-7', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Colossians 2:6-7 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "So then, just as you received Christ Jesus as Lord, continue to live your lives in him, rooted and built up in him, strengthened in the faith as you were taught, and overflowing with thankfulness." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Colossians 2:6-7, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Colossians 2:6-7. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that so then, just as you received christ jesus as lord, continue to live your lives in him, rooted and built up in him, strengthened in the faith as you were taught, and overflowing with thankfulness. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('3c8ef7f3-f2ed-43e4-93c7-6c6118913adc', 341, 'The Dwelling Place of God with Man', 3, 'Look! God’s dwelling place is now among the people, and he will dwell with them... He will wipe every tear from their eyes. There will be no more death or mourning or crying or pain.', 'Revelation 21:3-4', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Revelation 21:3-4 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "Look! God’s dwelling place is now among the people, and he will dwell with them... He will wipe every tear from their eyes. There will be no more death or mourning or crying or pain." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Revelation 21:3-4, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Revelation 21:3-4. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that look! god’s dwelling place is now among the people, and he will dwell with them... he will wipe every tear from their eyes. there will be no more death or mourning or crying or pain. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('7cd8be0d-4d50-4eec-9a46-27bf299e4bab', 342, 'The Soul\'s Unshakeable Anchor', 3, 'We have this hope as an anchor for the soul, firm and secure. It enters the inner sanctuary behind the curtain.', 'Hebrews 6:19', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Hebrews 6:19 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "We have this hope as an anchor for the soul, firm and secure. It enters the inner sanctuary behind the curtain." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Hebrews 6:19, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Hebrews 6:19. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that we have this hope as an anchor for the soul, firm and secure. it enters the inner sanctuary behind the curtain. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('334dae70-86ff-4202-a915-10087bd26f25', 343, 'Enduring Love That Outlasts Time', 3, 'Give thanks to the Lord, for he is good; his love endures forever.', 'Psalm 107:1', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Psalm 107:1 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "Give thanks to the Lord, for he is good; his love endures forever." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Psalm 107:1, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Psalm 107:1. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that give thanks to the lord, for he is good; his love endures forever. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('63f88f1c-d4a6-4dfc-a138-09dc4d31c348', 344, 'The Prince of Eternal Peace', 3, 'For to us a child is born, to us a son is given, and the government will be on his shoulders. And he will be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace.', 'Isaiah 9:6', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Isaiah 9:6 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "For to us a child is born, to us a son is given, and the government will be on his shoulders. And he will be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Isaiah 9:6, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Isaiah 9:6. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that for to us a child is born, to us a son is given, and the government will be on his shoulders. and he will be called wonderful counselor, mighty god, everlasting father, prince of peace. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('cebc3ada-4d2b-4edb-bea8-c88f821d2508', 345, 'A Living, Undying Hope', 3, 'Praise be to the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ! In his great mercy he has given us new birth into a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead.', '1 Peter 1:3', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of 1 Peter 1:3 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "Praise be to the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ! In his great mercy he has given us new birth into a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on 1 Peter 1:3, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in 1 Peter 1:3. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that praise be to the god and father of our lord jesus christ! in his great mercy he has given us new birth into a living hope through the resurrection of jesus christ from the dead. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('29f87647-3f95-4c04-9caf-8c1c94df1ee0', 346, 'Rejoicing on the Horizon of Dawn', 3, 'For his anger lasts only a moment, but his favor lasts a lifetime; weeping may stay for the night, but rejoicing comes in the morning.', 'Psalm 30:5', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Psalm 30:5 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "For his anger lasts only a moment, but his favor lasts a lifetime; weeping may stay for the night, but rejoicing comes in the morning." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Psalm 30:5, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Psalm 30:5. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that for his anger lasts only a moment, but his favor lasts a lifetime; weeping may stay for the night, but rejoicing comes in the morning. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('87dfd93c-3499-442f-adae-6b524e865168', 347, 'Glory Outweighing Present Trials', 3, 'I consider that our present sufferings are not worth comparing with the glory that will be revealed in us.', 'Romans 8:18', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Romans 8:18 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "I consider that our present sufferings are not worth comparing with the glory that will be revealed in us." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Romans 8:18, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Romans 8:18. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that i consider that our present sufferings are not worth comparing with the glory that will be revealed in us. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('cf6aa16f-373d-4b7d-9baf-4f036c4efd00', 348, 'The Eternal Weight of Glory', 3, 'Therefore we do not lose heart. Though outwardly we are wasting away, yet inwardly we are being renewed day by day. For our light and momentary troubles are achieving for us an eternal glory that far outweighs them all.', '2 Corinthians 4:16-17', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of 2 Corinthians 4:16-17 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "Therefore we do not lose heart. Though outwardly we are wasting away, yet inwardly we are being renewed day by day. For our light and momentary troubles are achieving for us an eternal glory that far outweighs them all." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on 2 Corinthians 4:16-17, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in 2 Corinthians 4:16-17. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that therefore we do not lose heart. though outwardly we are wasting away, yet inwardly we are being renewed day by day. for our light and momentary troubles are achieving for us an eternal glory that far outweighs them all. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('f56dd980-c660-42f4-a8ad-1e563528d015', 349, 'Citizens of the Unseen Kingdom', 3, 'But our citizenship is in heaven. And we eagerly await a Savior from there, the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Philippians 3:20', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Philippians 3:20 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "But our citizenship is in heaven. And we eagerly await a Savior from there, the Lord Jesus Christ." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Philippians 3:20, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Philippians 3:20. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that but our citizenship is in heaven. and we eagerly await a savior from there, the lord jesus christ. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('6a315419-c1b0-4774-b359-094cbe52e48b', 350, 'Rejoicing in This Very Day', 3, 'The Lord has done it this very day; let us rejoice today and be glad.', 'Psalm 118:24', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Psalm 118:24 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "The Lord has done it this very day; let us rejoice today and be glad." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Psalm 118:24, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Psalm 118:24. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that the lord has done it this very day; let us rejoice today and be glad. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.');
INSERT IGNORE INTO devotionals (id, day_number, title, duration_minutes, verse_text, verse_reference, reflection_text, prayer_text) VALUES
('16886d4c-6c48-40b6-9e6d-ca9ba7c1690e', 351, 'The Blessed Hope on the Horizon', 3, 'While we wait for the blessed hope—the appearing of the glory of our great God and Savior, Jesus Christ.', 'Titus 2:13', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Titus 2:13 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "While we wait for the blessed hope—the appearing of the glory of our great God and Savior, Jesus Christ." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Titus 2:13, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Titus 2:13. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that while we wait for the blessed hope—the appearing of the glory of our great god and savior, jesus christ. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('b0ed8e67-6579-42bd-8877-887e04605b68', 352, 'Always Abounding in Hope', 3, 'As for me, I will always have hope; I will praise you more and more.', 'Psalm 71:14', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Psalm 71:14 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "As for me, I will always have hope; I will praise you more and more." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Psalm 71:14, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Psalm 71:14. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that as for me, i will always have hope; i will praise you more and more. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('451b094a-29c1-4516-8f57-e9dba4b10a87', 353, 'Even So, Come Lord Jesus', 3, 'He who testifies to these things says, \'Yes, I am coming soon.\' Amen. Come, Lord Jesus.', 'Revelation 22:20', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Revelation 22:20 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "He who testifies to these things says, \'Yes, I am coming soon.\' Amen. Come, Lord Jesus." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Revelation 22:20, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Revelation 22:20. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that he who testifies to these things says, \'yes, i am coming soon.\' amen. come, lord jesus. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('2120b882-1ce9-407a-ac5a-881947df69ab', 354, 'Every Breath an Offering', 3, 'Let everything that has breath praise the Lord. Praise the Lord.', 'Psalm 150:6', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Psalm 150:6 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "Let everything that has breath praise the Lord. Praise the Lord." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Psalm 150:6, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Psalm 150:6. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that let everything that has breath praise the lord. praise the lord. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('b35d441f-4904-44e9-8edd-9d5d8c67f541', 355, 'Prepared by Infinite Love', 3, 'What no eye has seen, what no ear has heard, and what no human mind has conceived\'—the things God has prepared for those who love him.', '1 Corinthians 2:9', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of 1 Corinthians 2:9 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "What no eye has seen, what no ear has heard, and what no human mind has conceived\'—the things God has prepared for those who love him." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on 1 Corinthians 2:9, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in 1 Corinthians 2:9. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that what no eye has seen, what no ear has heard, and what no human mind has conceived\'—the things god has prepared for those who love him. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('5d337ac3-b7d6-4d4a-a5b6-f35ca24c05ac', 356, 'Praise Continually on the Lips', 3, 'I will extol the Lord at all times; his praise will always be on my lips.', 'Psalm 34:1', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Psalm 34:1 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "I will extol the Lord at all times; his praise will always be on my lips." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Psalm 34:1, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Psalm 34:1. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that i will extol the lord at all times; his praise will always be on my lips. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('729f9589-8046-44e3-83a8-da31ecc1e1bd', 357, 'Wait for the Appointed Dawn', 3, 'For the revelation awaits an appointed time; it speaks of the end and will not prove false. Though it linger, wait for it; it will certainly come and will not delay.', 'Habakkuk 2:3', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Habakkuk 2:3 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "For the revelation awaits an appointed time; it speaks of the end and will not prove false. Though it linger, wait for it; it will certainly come and will not delay." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Habakkuk 2:3, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Habakkuk 2:3. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that for the revelation awaits an appointed time; it speaks of the end and will not prove false. though it linger, wait for it; it will certainly come and will not delay. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('3127b614-9279-4d77-9965-2b30ccc7e8a2', 358, 'Peace to Hearts of Goodwill', 3, 'Glory to God in the highest heaven, and on earth peace to those on whom his favor rests.', 'Luke 2:14', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Luke 2:14 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "Glory to God in the highest heaven, and on earth peace to those on whom his favor rests." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Luke 2:14, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Luke 2:14. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that glory to god in the highest heaven, and on earth peace to those on whom his favor rests. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('2667b672-533d-4a80-be29-2f0d97d79bc2', 359, 'A Room Prepared in the Father\'s House', 3, 'Do not let your hearts be troubled. You believe in God; believe also in me. My Father’s house has many rooms... I am going there to prepare a place for you.', 'John 14:1-3', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of John 14:1-3 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "Do not let your hearts be troubled. You believe in God; believe also in me. My Father’s house has many rooms... I am going there to prepare a place for you." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on John 14:1-3, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in John 14:1-3. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that do not let your hearts be troubled. you believe in god; believe also in me. my father’s house has many rooms... i am going there to prepare a place for you. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('438a6b97-3f99-4a03-947b-c623395f2851', 360, 'Recounting His Wonders with All the Heart', 3, 'I will give thanks to you, Lord, with all my heart; I will tell of all your wonderful deeds.', 'Psalm 9:1', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Psalm 9:1 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "I will give thanks to you, Lord, with all my heart; I will tell of all your wonderful deeds." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Psalm 9:1, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Psalm 9:1. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that i will give thanks to you, lord, with all my heart; i will tell of all your wonderful deeds. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('4d413f25-cc31-4972-88de-37c565f64c54', 361, 'Inseparable from Sovereign Love', 3, 'For I am convinced that neither death nor life, neither angels nor demons, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers, neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.', 'Romans 8:38-39', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Romans 8:38-39 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "For I am convinced that neither death nor life, neither angels nor demons, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers, neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Romans 8:38-39, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Romans 8:38-39. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that for i am convinced that neither death nor life, neither angels nor demons, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers, neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of god that is in christ jesus our lord. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('b3699556-6596-4389-97d2-6d781b97e650', 362, 'Longing for the Heavenly City', 3, 'Instead, they were longing for a better country—a heavenly one. Therefore God is not ashamed to be called their God, for he has prepared a city for them.', 'Hebrews 11:16', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Hebrews 11:16 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "Instead, they were longing for a better country—a heavenly one. Therefore God is not ashamed to be called their God, for he has prepared a city for them." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Hebrews 11:16, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Hebrews 11:16. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that instead, they were longing for a better country—a heavenly one. therefore god is not ashamed to be called their god, for he has prepared a city for them. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('42bf23b0-4c65-43b4-aa93-6aa6e8d950b0', 363, 'Love at Morning, Faithfulness at Night', 3, 'It is good to praise the Lord and make music to your name, O Most High, proclaiming your love in the morning and your faithfulness at night.', 'Psalm 92:1-2', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Psalm 92:1-2 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "It is good to praise the Lord and make music to your name, O Most High, proclaiming your love in the morning and your faithfulness at night." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Psalm 92:1-2, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Psalm 92:1-2. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that it is good to praise the lord and make music to your name, o most high, proclaiming your love in the morning and your faithfulness at night. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('7fc8a787-2f2f-4d67-afc4-2a3a0bb7b173', 364, 'Behold, I Make All Things New', 3, 'He who was seated on the throne said, \'I am making everything new!\'', 'Revelation 21:5', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Revelation 21:5 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "He who was seated on the throne said, \'I am making everything new!\'" When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Revelation 21:5, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Revelation 21:5. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that he who was seated on the throne said, \'i am making everything new!\' Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.'),
('2b494086-4237-4cbd-9aba-021f86816b41', 365, 'Presented Faultless with Great Joy', 3, 'To him who is able to keep you from stumbling and to present you before his glorious presence without fault and with great joy—to the only God our Savior be glory, majesty, power and authority, through Jesus Christ our Lord, before all ages, now and forevermore! Amen.', 'Jude 1:24-25', 'In every season of life, God\'s Word arrives not merely as advice, but as a living anchor for the human soul. Today, in the context of unshakeable hope, gratitude & eternity, the truth of Jude 1:24-25 invites you to shift your focus away from momentary anxieties and onto the enduring character of God.\n\nConsider what is currently contending for your peace. Our natural inclination is often to strive in our own strength, to manage every outcome, or to replay yesterday\'s missteps. Yet scripture declares: "To him who is able to keep you from stumbling and to present you before his glorious presence without fault and with great joy—to the only God our Savior be glory, majesty, power and authority, through Jesus Christ our Lord, before all ages, now and forevermore! Amen." When you absorb this promise, your perspective transforms from human scarcity to heavenly abundance. God is already present in your tomorrow, orchestrating every circumstance with unfailing wisdom and grace.\n\n**Today\'s Interactive Practice:** Pause right now for sixty seconds. Inhale deeply through your nose, acknowledging God\'s breath in your lungs. As you slowly exhale, surrender the one situation you have been trying to control today. Whisper quietly: \'Lord, I trust Your heart, I stand on Jude 1:24-25, and I walk in Your peace.\'', 'Heavenly Father, I come before You today with an open heart, grateful for the living power of Your Word in Jude 1:24-25. Forgive me for the moments I allow worry or self-reliance to cloud my vision of Your goodness. Holy Spirit, anchor my thoughts in the truth that to him who is able to keep you from stumbling and to present you before his glorious presence without fault and with great joy—to the only god our savior be glory, majesty, power and authority, through jesus christ our lord, before all ages, now and forevermore! amen. Grant me discernment to recognize Your guidance, courage to walk by faith, and a spirit overflowed with gratitude. I dedicate my words, my work, and my relationships today to Your glory. In the mighty name of Jesus, Amen.');
INSERT IGNORE INTO declarations (id, day_number, scripture_text, scripture_reference, declaration_text, topic, gender) VALUES
('c3e309cb-2fae-4508-b45e-8108ac29ebe7', 1, 'Have I not commanded you? Be strong and courageous. Do not be afraid; do not be discouraged, for the Lord your God will be with you wherever you go.', 'Joshua 1:9', 'Fear has no dominion over my decisions. I step into every battle with warrior courage because the Lord of Hosts marches with me.', 'valentia', 'hombres'),
('c111befc-b804-45aa-b4dd-ecb30b4b3a33', 2, 'Be on your guard; stand firm in the faith; be courageous; be strong. Do everything in love.', '1 Corinthians 16:13', 'I stand guard over my convictions and my family. I am rooted in unshakeable faith and divine strength, acting with courageous love.', 'fortaleza', 'hombres'),
('cc1ddf1b-1f1b-433e-aa37-990f12de4b54', 3, 'But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit comes on you; and you will be my witnesses in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and to the ends of the earth.', 'Acts 1:8', 'I am baptized with supernatural power. The Holy Spirit empowers me to be a bold, unashamed witness for Jesus in my home, my city, and every sphere of influence.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('2c07b659-c9e7-4e04-8e42-0dd88e4bab8d', 4, 'As iron sharpens iron, so one person sharpens another.', 'Proverbs 27:17', 'I surround myself with godly brothers and speak wisdom into those I lead. We sharpen one another for Kingdom greatness.', 'liderazgo', 'hombres'),
('370b0403-8c6c-49f9-8466-6b122285287d', 5, 'Praise be to the Lord my Rock, who trains my hands for war, my fingers for battle.', 'Psalm 144:1', 'The Lord is my Rock and trainer in spiritual warfare. Through prayer and scripture, every enemy scheme formed against my house is broken.', 'batallas', 'hombres'),
('689056c6-49a2-4c4e-8a23-9e4da35fe682', 6, 'Finally, be strong in the Lord and in his mighty power. Put on the full armor of God, so that you can take your stand against the devil’s schemes.', 'Ephesians 6:10-11', 'I strap on the full armor of God daily. I do not fight in my own flesh, but stand immovable in the almighty power of Jesus Christ.', 'batallas', 'hombres'),
('bf66842b-0cf2-4b9e-bb28-54f9f1203557', 7, 'Join with me in suffering, like a good soldier of Christ Jesus.', '2 Timothy 2:3', 'I embrace discipline and sacrifice. Like a focused soldier, I refuse civilian distractions and run my race to please my King.', 'disciplina', 'hombres'),
('0b8c120c-3d23-46b5-ad48-7c5be96186c8', 8, 'But when he, the Spirit of truth, comes, he will guide you into all the truth. He will not speak on his own; he will speak only what he hears, and he will tell you what is yet to come.', 'John 16:13', 'The Spirit of Truth guides my every step. I do not walk in confusion or second-guessing; the Holy Spirit illuminates my path and reveals God’s wisdom to my spirit.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('7b64a28c-7d14-47e9-b29a-554af2a88a48', 9, 'It is God who arms me with strength and keeps my way secure.', 'Psalm 18:32', 'God equips my spirit with supernatural stamina. He clears my path of traps and keeps my footing firm on the heights.', 'fortaleza', 'hombres'),
('da4cfd69-312e-4129-a1cf-065b1b0a1fc4', 10, 'Trust in the Lord with all your heart and lean not on your own understanding; in all your ways submit to him, and he will make your paths straight.', 'Proverbs 3:5-6', 'I surrender my human logic to God\'s higher wisdom. In every business venture and life decision, He aligns my steps and straightens my path.', 'proposito', 'hombres'),
('f3eea718-5682-4c78-bf42-5a5f78da3c7f', 11, 'He has shown you, O mortal, what is good. And what does the Lord require of you? To act justly and to love mercy and to walk humbly with your God.', 'Micah 6:8', 'True manhood is found in humble obedience. I practice justice, extend mercy, and walk in reverent fellowship with my Creator.', 'identidad', 'hombres'),
('e1f328b5-8ff1-49af-af3f-751b64382aa1', 12, 'Whatever you do, work at it with all your heart, as working for the Lord, not for human masters.', 'Colossians 3:23', 'I execute my work with excellence, honor, and tireless diligence. I report directly to King Jesus, and His favor crowns my labor.', 'negocios', 'hombres'),
('e44e08fc-7237-4610-9ceb-6334b6ccdf27', 13, 'For those who are led by the Spirit of God are the children of God.', 'Romans 8:14', 'I am a true son of the living God, led daily by His Holy Spirit. My flesh does not dictate my direction; the Spirit guides my impulses, decisions, and heart.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('df149fea-006c-47d9-a1a0-a96c3b66cf2f', 14, 'Be alert and of sober mind. Your enemy the devil prowls around like a roaring lion looking for someone to devour. Resist him, standing firm in the faith.', '1 Peter 5:8-9', 'I stay spiritually vigilant and sober-minded. When the enemy roars, I roar back with the truth of God\'s Word and stand victorious.', 'valentia', 'hombres'),
('72a829d3-04dd-4774-82e0-ce201430b5a1', 15, 'But as for me and my household, we will serve the Lord.', 'Joshua 24:15', 'As the spiritual patriarch of my home, I make a holy decree: my house belongs to Jesus. We will honor, worship, and serve Him forever.', 'familia', 'hombres'),
('f28d3c30-df03-4b6d-9a0a-4f77b68ac61e', 16, 'The weapons we fight with are not the weapons of the world. On the contrary, they have divine power to demolish strongholds.', '2 Corinthians 10:4', 'I wield heavenly firepower through prayer, the Word, and faith. Mental strongholds, generational addictions, and fears are demolished.', 'batallas', 'hombres'),
('cbff23a1-566a-4cb7-86fa-f8ff240403ab', 17, 'Don’t be afraid of them. Remember the Lord, who is great and awesome, and fight for your families, your sons and your daughters, your wives and your homes.', 'Nehemiah 4:14', 'I will never back down when defending what God gave me. I fight in faith for my family, my marriage, and my legacy.', 'liderazgo', 'hombres'),
('4100cecb-bae8-47ad-b02b-bcb057499d56', 18, 'In the same way, the Spirit helps us in our weakness. We do not know what we ought to pray for, but the Spirit himself intercedes for us through wordless groans.', 'Romans 8:26', 'When I am weak or do not know what to pray, the Holy Spirit carries my petitions. His divine intercession aligns my prayers perfectly with the will of the Father.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('1045f386-0ecb-474d-9540-1f0671d97664', 19, 'Let us throw off everything that hinders and the sin that so easily entangles. And let us run with perseverance the race marked out for us, fixing our eyes on Jesus.', 'Hebrews 12:1-2', 'I cast away every weight and distraction. With my eyes locked onto Christ, I run my race with relentless grit and endurance.', 'fortaleza', 'hombres'),
('4185f2e0-4fa6-4e04-bd14-97cbd580ea70', 20, 'But remember the Lord your God, for it is he who gives you the ability to produce wealth.', 'Deuteronomy 8:18', 'God is the author of my capacity to create value and wealth. I manage His resources with wisdom, generosity, and Kingdom purpose.', 'provision', 'hombres'),
('07d35a0c-05cc-401c-a853-46e729c7ffe4', 21, 'Yet he did not waver through unbelief regarding the promise of God, but was strengthened in his faith and gave glory to God, being fully persuaded.', 'Romans 4:20-21', 'Like Abraham, I refuse to waver in doubt. God\'s promise is certain, and my faith gives Him immense glory as I wait on His fulfillment.', 'fe', 'hombres'),
('8ffe7441-6c8d-45e7-b858-fbc487b33b7b', 22, 'Though an army besiege me, my heart will not fear; though war break out against me, even then I will be confident.', 'Psalm 27:3', 'Surrounded by pressures and deadlines, my inner man remains at rest. The Peace of God rules like a sentinel in my soul.', 'paz', 'hombres'),
('b9d7447d-3682-4e2f-8a8d-d332ccbfd086', 23, 'But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, forbearance, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness and self-control. Against such things there is no law.', 'Galatians 5:22-23', 'The character of Jesus flourishes within me. By the Holy Spirit, I walk in supernatural love, unshakeable joy, and masculine self-control in every pressure.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('a129cfc5-7d22-4710-85aa-f6178523a821', 24, 'Praise the Lord, my soul, and forget not all his benefits—who forgives all your sins and heals all your diseases.', 'Psalm 103:2-3', 'God restores my physical vitality and mends my internal battles. I walk in divine health and renewed vigor to complete my assignment.', 'sanidad', 'hombres'),
('40b46d9e-5d97-45be-8b25-5c5fd8fdc9e6', 25, 'Enter his gates with thanksgiving and his courts with praise; give thanks to him and praise his name.', 'Psalm 100:4', 'I start my day by lifting up the Name of Jesus. A warrior\'s greatest weapon is a thankful spirit that praises God in advance of victory.', 'gratitud', 'hombres'),
('380846cd-d12d-4afc-b6ae-180f641794ae', 26, 'Have I not commanded you? Be strong and courageous. Do not be afraid; do not be discouraged, for the Lord your God will be with you wherever you go.', 'Joshua 1:9', 'Today I declare with authority: Fear has no dominion over my decisions. I step into every battle with warrior courage because the Lord of Hosts marches with me.', 'valentia', 'hombres'),
('07ad9e93-fd01-4b64-b79a-afb787921914', 27, 'Be on your guard; stand firm in the faith; be courageous; be strong. Do everything in love.', '1 Corinthians 16:13', 'Today I declare with authority: I stand guard over my convictions and my family. I am rooted in unshakeable faith and divine strength, acting with courageous love.', 'fortaleza', 'hombres'),
('cb7b745c-5a48-4274-a25c-cd9a284edb4a', 28, 'Do you not know that your bodies are temples of the Holy Spirit, who is in you, whom you have received from God? You are not your own; you were bought at a price.', '1 Corinthians 6:19-20', 'My body is a holy sanctuary of the Spirit of God. I honor God with my eyes, my thoughts, and my physical strength, refusing every snare of impurity.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('82e251da-b914-4736-ae71-f2a26864f855', 29, 'As iron sharpens iron, so one person sharpens another.', 'Proverbs 27:17', 'Today I declare with authority: I surround myself with godly brothers and speak wisdom into those I lead. We sharpen one another for Kingdom greatness.', 'liderazgo', 'hombres'),
('a7a941be-b0ee-433f-80de-f7f10e1355f5', 30, 'Praise be to the Lord my Rock, who trains my hands for war, my fingers for battle.', 'Psalm 144:1', 'Today I declare with authority: The Lord is my Rock and trainer in spiritual warfare. Through prayer and scripture, every enemy scheme formed against my house is broken.', 'batallas', 'hombres'),
('f36384b5-a8c8-4358-893d-88627cda9060', 31, 'Finally, be strong in the Lord and in his mighty power. Put on the full armor of God, so that you can take your stand against the devil’s schemes.', 'Ephesians 6:10-11', 'Today I declare with authority: I strap on the full armor of God daily. I do not fight in my own flesh, but stand immovable in the almighty power of Jesus Christ.', 'batallas', 'hombres'),
('b6c1a27b-722a-4cf8-9688-3b3441a191d7', 32, 'Join with me in suffering, like a good soldier of Christ Jesus.', '2 Timothy 2:3', 'Today I declare with authority: I embrace discipline and sacrifice. Like a focused soldier, I refuse civilian distractions and run my race to please my King.', 'disciplina', 'hombres'),
('42a970cc-2461-4732-9a36-1f9bcd7d9c84', 33, 'For the Spirit God gave us does not make us timid, but gives us power, love and self-discipline.', '2 Timothy 1:7', 'Timidity and cowardice have no room in my soul. The Holy Spirit fuels me with holy courage, boundless agape love, and laser-sharp self-mastery.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('42976523-f411-4bfe-a8b5-81d06462ec4e', 34, 'It is God who arms me with strength and keeps my way secure.', 'Psalm 18:32', 'Today I declare with authority: God equips my spirit with supernatural stamina. He clears my path of traps and keeps my footing firm on the heights.', 'fortaleza', 'hombres'),
('fbdf1d56-cc70-4456-94e5-36402cb62646', 35, 'Trust in the Lord with all your heart and lean not on your own understanding; in all your ways submit to him, and he will make your paths straight.', 'Proverbs 3:5-6', 'Today I declare with authority: I surrender my human logic to God\'s higher wisdom. In every business venture and life decision, He aligns my steps and straightens my path.', 'proposito', 'hombres'),
('7ed1d478-3892-40d5-a6aa-94a61280d09f', 36, 'He has shown you, O mortal, what is good. And what does the Lord require of you? To act justly and to love mercy and to walk humbly with your God.', 'Micah 6:8', 'Today I declare with authority: True manhood is found in humble obedience. I practice justice, extend mercy, and walk in reverent fellowship with my Creator.', 'identidad', 'hombres'),
('079033c3-4a63-46a7-a8cb-71ecba84fa81', 37, 'Whatever you do, work at it with all your heart, as working for the Lord, not for human masters.', 'Colossians 3:23', 'Today I declare with authority: I execute my work with excellence, honor, and tireless diligence. I report directly to King Jesus, and His favor crowns my labor.', 'negocios', 'hombres'),
('eb70c0a5-ff66-415d-94ab-b89969c15308', 38, 'Now the Lord is the Spirit, and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is freedom.', '2 Corinthians 3:17', 'Where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is absolute freedom. Every chain of addiction, fear, and condemnation is broken off my life today.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('76bba43e-b06a-44c2-84b8-aacb95420024', 39, 'Be alert and of sober mind. Your enemy the devil prowls around like a roaring lion looking for someone to devour. Resist him, standing firm in the faith.', '1 Peter 5:8-9', 'Today I declare with authority: I stay spiritually vigilant and sober-minded. When the enemy roars, I roar back with the truth of God\'s Word and stand victorious.', 'valentia', 'hombres'),
('2fcfb6f3-6a27-4fa8-aa1f-2cbd5c6f131e', 40, 'But as for me and my household, we will serve the Lord.', 'Joshua 24:15', 'Today I declare with authority: As the spiritual patriarch of my home, I make a holy decree: my house belongs to Jesus. We will honor, worship, and serve Him forever.', 'familia', 'hombres'),
('6e14c08e-8bb0-4a5e-8c1a-158fdaa0998a', 41, 'The weapons we fight with are not the weapons of the world. On the contrary, they have divine power to demolish strongholds.', '2 Corinthians 10:4', 'Today I declare with authority: I wield heavenly firepower through prayer, the Word, and faith. Mental strongholds, generational addictions, and fears are demolished.', 'batallas', 'hombres'),
('a826bfc6-d089-459b-8018-685aa4a5995d', 42, 'Don’t be afraid of them. Remember the Lord, who is great and awesome, and fight for your families, your sons and your daughters, your wives and your homes.', 'Nehemiah 4:14', 'Today I declare with authority: I will never back down when defending what God gave me. I fight in faith for my family, my marriage, and my legacy.', 'liderazgo', 'hombres'),
('8296b10a-a979-4b0b-b067-274d161b0a62', 43, 'The Spirit of the Lord is on me, because he has anointed me to proclaim good news to the poor. He has sent me to proclaim freedom for the prisoners and recovery of sight for the blind.', 'Luke 4:18-19', 'The anointing of the Holy Spirit rests upon my life. I am empowered to proclaim liberty, bring healing to wounded hearts, and advance the Kingdom of God with authority.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('e899e6e5-da31-4425-a7df-5ab7ccec145a', 44, 'Let us throw off everything that hinders and the sin that so easily entangles. And let us run with perseverance the race marked out for us, fixing our eyes on Jesus.', 'Hebrews 12:1-2', 'Today I declare with authority: I cast away every weight and distraction. With my eyes locked onto Christ, I run my race with relentless grit and endurance.', 'fortaleza', 'hombres'),
('04a2a25d-938f-4475-88de-30e2f2b5ff1b', 45, 'But remember the Lord your God, for it is he who gives you the ability to produce wealth.', 'Deuteronomy 8:18', 'Today I declare with authority: God is the author of my capacity to create value and wealth. I manage His resources with wisdom, generosity, and Kingdom purpose.', 'provision', 'hombres'),
('5df36ed2-a962-4b08-90dc-becffe9b6e8b', 46, 'Yet he did not waver through unbelief regarding the promise of God, but was strengthened in his faith and gave glory to God, being fully persuaded.', 'Romans 4:20-21', 'Today I declare with authority: Like Abraham, I refuse to waver in doubt. God\'s promise is certain, and my faith gives Him immense glory as I wait on His fulfillment.', 'fe', 'hombres'),
('c7558fb2-700b-4a5c-90fc-77788327a588', 47, 'Though an army besiege me, my heart will not fear; though war break out against me, even then I will be confident.', 'Psalm 27:3', 'Today I declare with authority: Surrounded by pressures and deadlines, my inner man remains at rest. The Peace of God rules like a sentinel in my soul.', 'paz', 'hombres'),
('cd02b5af-e4a2-4a0b-a857-0d1e9b31ecb7', 48, 'And you also were included in Christ when you heard the message of truth... having believed, you were marked in him with a seal, the promised Holy Spirit.', 'Ephesians 1:13-14', 'I am sealed for eternity by the Holy Spirit of promise. My inheritance is guaranteed, my salvation is secure, and my identity in Christ is untouchable.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('413e7169-2ccd-4c29-be81-61818c281827', 49, 'Praise the Lord, my soul, and forget not all his benefits—who forgives all your sins and heals all your diseases.', 'Psalm 103:2-3', 'Today I declare with authority: God restores my physical vitality and mends my internal battles. I walk in divine health and renewed vigor to complete my assignment.', 'sanidad', 'hombres'),
('75d8b0aa-6753-46b0-8d44-549fefb432cf', 50, 'Enter his gates with thanksgiving and his courts with praise; give thanks to him and praise his name.', 'Psalm 100:4', 'Today I declare with authority: I start my day by lifting up the Name of Jesus. A warrior\'s greatest weapon is a thankful spirit that praises God in advance of victory.', 'gratitud', 'hombres');
INSERT IGNORE INTO declarations (id, day_number, scripture_text, scripture_reference, declaration_text, topic, gender) VALUES
('c399f895-72bd-4a05-8fe1-10e6f5b46368', 51, 'Have I not commanded you? Be strong and courageous. Do not be afraid; do not be discouraged, for the Lord your God will be with you wherever you go.', 'Joshua 1:9', 'Standing on the Word: Fear has no dominion over my decisions. I step into every battle with warrior courage because the Lord of Hosts marches with me.', 'valentia', 'hombres'),
('2f9cf5ac-7673-4249-b3fa-6bbf697d7efd', 52, 'Be on your guard; stand firm in the faith; be courageous; be strong. Do everything in love.', '1 Corinthians 16:13', 'Standing on the Word: I stand guard over my convictions and my family. I am rooted in unshakeable faith and divine strength, acting with courageous love.', 'fortaleza', 'hombres'),
('1e255291-5f00-4bd2-8558-8c64b6d45b4d', 53, 'The Spirit of the Lord will rest on him—the Spirit of wisdom and of understanding, the Spirit of counsel and of might, the Spirit of the knowledge and fear of the Lord.', 'Isaiah 11:2', 'The sevenfold Spirit of God rests upon me: wisdom for decisions, understanding for complex matters, counsel in uncertainty, and supernatural might for the battle.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('7e655f5b-c6ca-4de9-9f68-b7cdc6873d53', 54, 'As iron sharpens iron, so one person sharpens another.', 'Proverbs 27:17', 'Standing on the Word: I surround myself with godly brothers and speak wisdom into those I lead. We sharpen one another for Kingdom greatness.', 'liderazgo', 'hombres'),
('01424f12-1d3d-4e5a-a80f-fc3f06db4a85', 55, 'Praise be to the Lord my Rock, who trains my hands for war, my fingers for battle.', 'Psalm 144:1', 'Standing on the Word: The Lord is my Rock and trainer in spiritual warfare. Through prayer and scripture, every enemy scheme formed against my house is broken.', 'batallas', 'hombres'),
('acc451db-5631-4a62-81f3-82e0b31b059e', 56, 'Finally, be strong in the Lord and in his mighty power. Put on the full armor of God, so that you can take your stand against the devil’s schemes.', 'Ephesians 6:10-11', 'Standing on the Word: I strap on the full armor of God daily. I do not fight in my own flesh, but stand immovable in the almighty power of Jesus Christ.', 'batallas', 'hombres'),
('7a967613-66bb-4abb-bb00-cc160faea79c', 57, 'Join with me in suffering, like a good soldier of Christ Jesus.', '2 Timothy 2:3', 'Standing on the Word: I embrace discipline and sacrifice. Like a focused soldier, I refuse civilian distractions and run my race to please my King.', 'disciplina', 'hombres'),
('22f5e52f-7fe8-4229-81dc-c09dd7df6805', 58, 'Whoever believes in me, as Scripture has said, rivers of living water will flow from within them. By this he meant the Spirit, whom those who believed in him were later to receive.', 'John 7:38-39', 'Rivers of living water surge from my innermost being. The Holy Spirit refreshes my soul, revives my home, and brings spiritual vitality wherever I go.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('88b62ff7-0ebc-4fd8-bfcc-9c9cace0d2ec', 59, 'It is God who arms me with strength and keeps my way secure.', 'Psalm 18:32', 'Standing on the Word: God equips my spirit with supernatural stamina. He clears my path of traps and keeps my footing firm on the heights.', 'fortaleza', 'hombres'),
('99e0112f-9432-4ba6-b825-6450291a08a6', 60, 'Trust in the Lord with all your heart and lean not on your own understanding; in all your ways submit to him, and he will make your paths straight.', 'Proverbs 3:5-6', 'Standing on the Word: I surrender my human logic to God\'s higher wisdom. In every business venture and life decision, He aligns my steps and straightens my path.', 'proposito', 'hombres'),
('15ddfb2d-bf4c-4dd0-964d-bf8572c7b999', 61, 'He has shown you, O mortal, what is good. And what does the Lord require of you? To act justly and to love mercy and to walk humbly with your God.', 'Micah 6:8', 'Standing on the Word: True manhood is found in humble obedience. I practice justice, extend mercy, and walk in reverent fellowship with my Creator.', 'identidad', 'hombres'),
('621ee7cf-2eae-48a3-af08-0d0005531ff6', 62, 'Whatever you do, work at it with all your heart, as working for the Lord, not for human masters.', 'Colossians 3:23', 'Standing on the Word: I execute my work with excellence, honor, and tireless diligence. I report directly to King Jesus, and His favor crowns my labor.', 'negocios', 'hombres'),
('29372b99-67b1-48d4-8392-b22cf345b414', 63, 'May the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace as you trust in him, so that you may overflow with hope by the power of the Holy Spirit.', 'Romans 15:13', 'I overflow with vibrant hope today through the power of the Holy Spirit. Despair is cast out, and divine optimism anchors my heart.', 'holy_spirit', 'hombres'),
('d93738c2-ff72-47d0-b2ce-d071747bf4d7', 64, 'Be alert and of sober mind. Your enemy the devil prowls around like a roaring lion looking for someone to devour. Resist him, standing firm in the faith.', '1 Peter 5:8-9', 'Standing on the Word: I stay spiritually vigilant and sober-minded. When the enemy roars, I roar back with the truth of God\'s Word and stand victorious.', 'valentia', 'hombres'),
('e8bfb5f2-79bc-4131-bc85-e6b19eefd9d6', 65, 'But as for me and my household, we will serve the Lord.', 'Joshua 24:15', 'Standing on the Word: As the spiritual patriarch of my home, I make a holy decree: my house belongs to Jesus. We will honor, worship, and serve Him forever.', 'familia', 'hombres'),
